{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560297-v20-multiple-merits-and-flaws-questions","id":1560297,"title":"[V20] Multiple merits and flaws questions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-05-31T19:44:04-07:00","id":1560297,"title":"[V20] Multiple merits and flaws questions","content":"Greetings,<br /> <br /> Some questions arise, and I would like help for V20:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>V20 Core p. 479</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">A character may take as many Mer\u00ad-<br /> its as the player can afford, but no character may have<br /> more than seven points\u2019 worth of Flaws</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> However I keep finding exceptions to that statement:<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>V20 Lore of the Clans p. 126</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Light within Shadow<br /> ...<br /> If<br /> they fail, they may try again the next night, but if they<br /> botch they permanently gain the Uncontrollable Night<br /> Sight Flaw (p. 123).<br /> ...<br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> \u200b<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>V20 Lore of the Clans p. 127</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Commune with the Abyss<br /> ...<br /> They also permanently<br /> gain the Nightmares Flaw (V20, p. 485).\u200b<br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> \u200b\u200b<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>V20 Lore of the Bloodlines p. 60</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Necromancy Lie<br /> At the Storyteller\u2019s discretion, Kiasyd may<br /> take the Discipline of Necromancy instead<br /> of Dominate, but in so doing earn the Clan<br /> Enmity Flaw (V20, p. 492) twice, both for the<br /> Giovanni and Harbingers of Skulls. Freebie<br /> points aren\u2019t gained for taking these Flaws\u200b.<br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> <br /> <br /> So, is it possible at character generation and normal game play, to have someone with more than 7 dots of flaws (I am not asking for freebies, just someone with several flaws that make sense for the concept).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 05-31-2026, 10:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-31T20:30:49-07:00","id":1560298,"title":"","content":"The phrasing in V20 allows for two readings as I can tell:<br /> <br /> In both, you can only start with 7 points of Flaws during creation. In play, either you can gain as many more as the ST feels is appropriate (point values cease to matter in play anyway, Merits and Flaws are gains/lost at ST discretion), or you're capped at 7 and the ST would have to remove some to make room for another if gaining more is on the table.<br /> <br /> That said, I haven't been in a normal TT game where we haven't done a house rule of, &quot;you can have as many Flaws as you want, but max 7 bonus freebies at creation&quot; over following the strict 7 cap set out in the book. Since they can be removed by fiat anyway, if everyone's wrong at gen and characters are crippled by Flaws, that can be fixed in play. If a character is just a better combo of flavor and mechanics at 8 or 9 dots worth of Flaws than 7... it doesn't hurt anyone if the impact on creation resources stays capped.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-31T23:20:57-07:00","id":1560299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560297-v20-multiple-merits-and-flaws-questions?p=1560298#post1560298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, I haven't been in a normal TT game where we haven't done a house rule of, &quot;you can have as many Flaws as you want, but max 7 bonus freebies at creation&quot; over following the strict 7 cap set out in the book.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, I just realized that's a house rule. I've always been playing that way. Players can take an unlimited number of flaws at character creation but can only gain a max of 7 points. And once the game starts they can gain an unlimited number of merits or flaws but it's generally up to the ST to decide whether they get those. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-01T12:59:26-07:00","id":1560305,"title":"","content":"I can appreciate the logic of the cap. For people newer to the Merit/Flaw mechanics it can be really easy to go overboard with them. As well in non-TT style play (like large group play that still uses the TT rules) where there's just more people and thus more expectations to juggle, having the cap can be for the best. For sitting around with friends that all know each other? It's very easy to drop it. But that's why it's so common it turns into one of the technically a house rule people forgot was a house rule incidents. With a bit of the wording between editions varying a bit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-02T09:39:19-07:00","id":1560311,"title":"","content":"Thanks for your replies <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar741_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"741\" data-vbnamecard=\"741\">AnubisXy</a><br /> <br /> It is specially interesting as M20 Book of Secrets makes the limit for mages, up to 13 dots of flaws for starting characters.<br /> <br /> And certain character concepts benefit from flaws, my favourites are the social ones that can be used to tell an interesting narrative.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-02T11:36:19-07:00","id":1560313,"title":"","content":"While speculation, I think M20 did that to compensate for including the huge number of Backgrounds inherited from MRev, but cutting the Adversarial Backgrounds as an addition to Flaws to get more points to spend.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-02T18:38:04-07:00","id":1560316,"title":"","content":"I believe it means you can only have 7 points worth of Flaws at character creation, to prevent players from buffing the hell out of their characters by taking a bunch of non-issue flaws for extra Freebies.<br /> <br /> Once you get out of character creation, it seems to be free game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-21T05:52:00-07:00","id":1560815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560297-v20-multiple-merits-and-flaws-questions?p=1560305#post1560305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can appreciate the logic of the cap. For people newer to the Merit/Flaw mechanics it can be really easy to go overboard with them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I end up needing the hard cap in my games because I have a couple players with Anxiety problems that specifically handle creation as &quot;everything has to have a strict mechanic attached to it or I'll be cheating&quot;. They have a hard time with the idea of unbounded fluff.<br /> <br /> So if I don't step in they'll get 70% of the book in Flaws and Merits that don't really matter, for minor attached fluff, and end up with unplayable sheets.<br /> <br /> Getting better, but for now hard stop it is, giving them space backfired every single time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}